  "clause": "DESIGN R3.3 \u00a710.1 serializePrepared; \u00a710.2 OPEN-EXPORT-EVIDENCE",
  "witness": "a node parented to another node keeps that parent in the serialized cells",
  "derivation": "prepared = export.map.grid-fixture payload (writer = grid exports[0].serializer): diagram e_10 First sheet with cells e_12 'First on first' (layer) and e_13 'Last on first' parented to e_12 in IR emission order (e_12 then e_13 after the other page's node); diagram e_11 Second sheet with e_14 'Second view'. DESIGN R3.3 fixes no draw.io bytes (structural until engine goldens, OPEN-EXPORT-EVIDENCE), so the payload bytes and digest are UNSEALED and checked structurally with the shared drawio-structure/1 projection (harmonization L3): one diagram per IR page in IR order with id and name; inside each, every mxCell with vertex='1' or edge='1' in document order as {id, kind, parent, value?, source?, target?} (parent equal to the diagram layer cell written $layer; a node carries its IR name as value, an edge its IR name and endpoints, a label record is a vertex whose value is its text); byte invariants UTF-8 without BOM, no CR (newline LF), no compression (none), no paired empty element (short), digest = B(bytes); a second call returns identical bytes. Geometry and style attributes are not compared (DESIGN R3.3 pins no draw.io unit or style mapping). The Result echoes the preparation identity and revision; its report carries the prepared report entries and idMap and one artifact record whose digest is B(bytes) and whose entryIndexes list every entry (parity sync PS-26: the download context carries the full report, DESIGN \u00a78.1.1 L621; every loss stays reachable through entryIndexes, \u00a710.1 L753; downloads consume the Result directly, \u00a710.2 L803).",
